{
 "module": "scene",
 "storyboard": "films/scene/saas-hero-launch.storyboard.md",
 "_template": "FILLABLE TEMPLATE - a white-first SaaS launch film. Nothing here is anyone's brand: the product is the fictional 'Meridian', every colour is a theme token, and every logo in the wall is invented. To reskin, change `theme` (any file in themes/) and nothing else. To refill, replace the copy strings, the logoWall entries, the browserFrame rows, the barChart data and the four capability cards. Structure, timing and camera are the part worth keeping.",
 "orientation": "landscape",
 "theme": "default",
 "duration": 45,
 "audio": {
  "silent": true,
  "_why": "Template ships mute so a fork can drop its own bed in without fighting a mix it did not choose. Replace with a real audio block before shipping."
 },
 "_camera": "The camera is written as MOVES, not keys: the generators in core/camera-moves.js own the arithmetic, so retiming a beat is one number. The dive is the only large one, and it lands on the release panel because that is the beat the film is about. A dive is bounded by the copy it must not push off the frame. At scale s centred on tx the left edge of the visible stage is tx - 960/s, and both films set their text column at x=150, so tx must stay at or under 150 + 960/s. The first pass dove to 1.2 on the panel centre and cropped the whole left column for five seconds with every gate green; `make judge` was the only thing that saw it.",
 "_cuts": "One family, soft: this is a white editorial film and a punchy edit would fight it. `blur` and `riseBlur` are the two soft styles that work without beat wrapping (core/cuts.js refuses a masking cut on a whole-frame root, because there is nothing underneath to reveal). Each cut sits in the gap between two beats, and the backdrop windows below carry no times because they bind to these joints (core/junctions.js).",
 "spectacle": {
  "at": 26.5,
  "of": "shippedTotal",
  "device": "cinematicZoom",
  "why": "The film has spent 24 seconds showing ONE release go out. The peak lands where the counter stops, not where the beat opens: a 0.9s sting written at the cut buried the number's whole entrance, so it is written where 4.8M settles instead. The device is monochrome on purpose. `chromaticSplit` was tried and painted a rainbow ring over the chart, which is off-palette on a film whose whole look is one blue. It is the only beat allowed to raise its voice."
 },
